a.q('full_standards_payload',['method_reference_payload'],'Install full source-distribution standards tree, including templates/secondary surfaces; a representative test minimum does not reduce that obligation. Manifest records source/root and copied inventory or checksums. Reference docs needed by cold agents appear in product/installer manifests without downstream HOW. Installed standards remain reference payloads and do not outrank upstream specification_methodology for shared-law editing.',[g(2,176,193)])
a.c('cold_agent_bootstrap','Cold-agent bootstrap','Prior-memory-free discovery of installed substrate, command bindings, method references and workspace ownership boundary, with versioned ABG/GTL context under target .abiogenesis recorded in manifest/provenance.',[g(3,197,213)])
a.q('bootstrap_idempotence_and_ownership',['cold_agent_bootstrap'],'Keep substrate instructions domain-neutral and downstream-specific sections visibly separate. Installer delivery is marker-governed or otherwise idempotent. Fresh/same-identity refresh updates product-owned context in AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md idempotently preserving unrelated project guidance; malformed paired markers fail closed. Downstream need not hand-edit semantic compression; selected product replaces stale owned sections. Bootstrap binds shared version via .abiogenesis and only provides local references/context/state initialization; product payload materializes at shared toolchain, not per downstream workspace.',[g(3,202,231)])
